abstract: >-
  MicroRT-Lab is a deterministic discrete-event simulation laboratory for
  operating-system scheduling and synchronization concepts. Workloads are
  described in JSON; a C++ engine executes them tick-by-tick and produces
  complete, reproducible result documents (event traces, Gantt timelines,
  per-task accounting, metrics, deadlock reports, memory statistics).
  A Python analysis layer manages experiments, recomputes metrics as an
  independent cross-check, compares scheduler variants and generates
  reports; a web workstation visualizes everything with playback,
  resource-allocation graphs and memory maps.
